{
  "title": "Dagger engine heap: what the open memory PRs take out of it (measured)",
  "subtitle": "Real engines, one at a time: BEFORE = main @ 0120da0, AFTER = memory-fixes-combined-lease @ 40f41ce (0120da0 + #15202 #15215 #15216 #15212 #15213 #15223 #15224 #15226 #15218 #15219 #15220 #15221 #15232). The same scripted agent (no LLM) drives one `dagger mcp` session on each for 290 turns: reads, edits, go build/vet/test with test spans, growing tool state, module loads, trace inspection.",
  "caption": "Measured at turn 290: 5.14 GiB -\u003e 4.01 GiB of pprof in-use heap (-22%); HeapInuse 7.2 -\u003e 5.6 GB. BEFORE was stopped at turn 290 by a memory cap (Sys \u003e 14 GiB), not a time limit. Growth over the second half: 24.7 -\u003e 18.7 MiB/turn. Dang prepared dirs, arbitrary results, content-hash trees and the telemetry indexes shrink as the PRs intend; schema building does not, because this single agent loads a new module every turn (see note 4).",
